.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# ─── Obsidian UI/session state (not content) ───
# We ship the canonical .obsidian/app.json + .obsidian/graph.json so new clones
# inherit the spine filter and core settings. Obsidian then writes a bunch of
# additional files as it runs — workspace layout, theme state, cache, plugin
# state — which churn on every open and pollute git diffs. Ignore those.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspace.json.bak
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/appearance.json
.obsidian/core-plugins.json
.obsidian/core-plugins-migration.json
.obsidian/community-plugins.json
.obsidian/hotkeys.json
.obsidian/types.json
.obsidian/templates.json
.obsidian/canvas.json
.obsidian/bookmarks.json
.obsidian/daily-notes.json
.obsidian/page-preview.json
.obsidian/zk-prefixer.json
.obsidian/note-composer.json
.obsidian/command-palette.json
.obsidian/file-recovery.json
.obsidian/switcher.json
.obsidian/plugins/
.obsidian/themes/
.obsidian/snippets/

# Ignore the two configs Obsidian writes-back on every graph interaction.
# Canonical defaults live in system/.obsidian-defaults/ and are copied to
# .obsidian/ on first vault open (see README → "Getting started" → "5. Open in
# Obsidian"). After the first copy, your local play with the graph (zoom,
# colors, layout) doesn't pollute git.
.obsidian/graph.json
.obsidian/app.json

# ─── Editor + OS noise ───
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db

# ─── Outputs / scratch ───
# Anything in outputs/ at the repo root is treated as ephemeral session work,
# not vault content. (The /system/scripts/ folder is the canonical home for
# scripts that ship with the kit.)
outputs/

# ─── Python script cache ───
__pycache__/
*.pyc
system/scripts/__pycache__/
system/backlinks.json
